enchilada: MSS: boot the modem DSP through MBA/RMB in gated stages (mss=2..5, Wi-Fi round 2)

Wi-Fi needs the modem (wlanmdsp.mbn runs on it), and SDM845 MSS is MBA self-auth
(qcom,pil-self-auth), not SCM PAS. With mss>=2 the 0210 probe runs as before and, if it was clean
(SMEM v12, apps-mpss and global partitions valid, no region overlap), a kernel thread follows
Linux v6.12 qcom_q6v5_mss.c for sdm845_mss (has_alt_reset, no spare/qaccept/ext regs). Each stage
is a prefix of the next, ends in one "SWEET MSS: stage N: ok/FAILED: ..." line, and any failure
runs the stop path; one attempt per boot.
2: modem.mdt, mba.mbn and the 25 modem.bNN files are read from modem_a (UFS LUN 4, 0260) at the
byte offsets of a table made from modem_a.img by tools/mss-fw-table.py; every file's crc32 must
match before anything else happens. The mdt is checked as q6v5_mpss_load would (ELF32, phdr 0 not
PT_LOAD, header + hash = the whole 8412-byte mdt, every loadable segment inside mpss 0x8e000000 +
0x7800000, filesz <= memsz, each bNN in the table with the phdr's size). Item 435 or 428 present =
the modem is not cold: refused. Then SMP2P item 428 is allocated as qcom_smem_alloc_private does
(apps-mpss partition, TCSR mutex 3) and filled as qcom_smp2p_alloc_outbound_item does (pid 0->1,
16 entries, SSR_ACK, outbound "master-kernel" and "ipa", version 1 last), and the modem is kicked
(apss_shared+0xc bit 14).
3: assign_mem is checked with IS_CALL_AVAIL; mba.mbn is copied to the MBA region 0x96600000 (the
phone's DT; mainline has 0x96500000) through a 512 KiB write-combined window and read back; MPSS
and then MBA are assigned HLOS -> MSS_MSA RW (SVC_MP 0xc cmd 0x16, arginfo 0x1117, buffers in a
plain-RAM scratch page at 0xa1000000 laid out like Linux's, args 3-6 in the x5 block; INTERRUPTED
calls resumed with x0=1, x1-x5 again, x6 kept, x7=0; EBUSY retried 3x). With mss=3 both are
reclaimed and the MBA bytes read back again.
4: QMP opened (qmp_open handshake, polled) and "load_state modem on" sent; ACTIVE votes cx, mx,
mss at their top corner (0261); prng, then iface and snoc_axi on; q6v5_reset_deassert with
alt-reset (PDC sync reset bit 9, RMB+0x44, AOSS MSS_RESTART pulse); bus, mem, gpll0_mss, mnoc_axi
on; RMB_MBA_IMAGE = MBA; QDSP6SS sleep CBCR, BOOT_CORE_START, BOOT_CMD, boot FSM; PBL status must
be 1 within 1 s and MBA status 1 or 2 within 5 s.
5: RMB validator reset; metadata (= the mdt) assigned to the modem, META_DATA_READY, status 3
within 1 s, metadata reclaimed; MPSS reclaimed then shared; each segment streamed from modem_a
into MPSS (tails zeroed), PMI code start + LOAD_READY on the first, the cumulative length after
each, a negative status stops; MPSS assigned to the modem; AUTH_COMPLETE (4) within 10 s; the
modem's item 435 "slave-kernel" ready bit within 5 s; MBA reclaimed; 60 s watch of slave-kernel
(a fatal prints item 421); then a graceful stop (master-kernel stop bit, stop-ack up to 5 s).
Stop path (q6v5_stop/q6v5_mba_reclaim order): stop request if running, AXI halt of q6/modem/nc
(TCSR 0x1f63000/0x1f65000/0x1f64000), reset assert, our clock enables cleared (bits that were on
before are left on), MBA and metadata reclaimed, MPSS reclaimed only if the Q6 never ran (Linux
leaves it), load_state off, mss.lvl off; cx/mx stay voted because the apps DRV's earlier vote is
unknown. No XO proxy vote (the apps CPU runs from XO). Accesses are fenced: registers only on
fixed pages, stores only to the listed registers, QDSP6SS/RMB only once the rails and iface are
on, SMEM stores only inside the apps-mpss partition, carve-out windows only while HLOS owns them
and dropped before every assign. Without mss or with mss=0/1 the kernel is the 0210 one.

